course: dictionary
lesson: 1229
title: Strong words, strong meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have one meaning in a science book and another meaning in everyday talk. Bulletproof means strong enough to stop bullets from going through, like a bulletproof vest or bulletproof glass.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «a bulletproof plan» to mean a plan that is very strong and sure not to fail. The context tells you which meaning is used. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about bullets, or about how sure something is?
explain: Read the words around the word. «Some believed their rituals made them bulletproof.» The word «believed» is a clue: it shows people thought something was true, which does not always mean it really was. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Bulletproof is an adjective, a word that describes a noun.
fact: «Bulletproof» means strong enough to stop bullets from going through.
fact: In everyday talk, «bulletproof» can mean very reliable or certain, as in «a bulletproof plan».
fact: Common phrases include bulletproof vest, bulletproof glass and bulletproof car.
fact: «The Boxers» attacked foreigners and Chinese Christians in 1899–1901, and some believed their rituals made them bulletproof.
exercise: Police officers wear a «bulletproof vest». What does bulletproof mean here? | Very wet and slippery | Good for dancing | Made of soft cloth | *Strong enough to stop bullets from going through
exercise: Nadia says her plan is «bulletproof». What does this suggest? | It is a plan for a rainy day | It is very long and complicated | *Very strong and certain, so it is unlikely to fail | It has holes that bullets can go through
exercise: «Some believed their rituals made them bulletproof.» Why is the word «believed» a useful clue? | *It shows people thought it, which does not always mean it was true | It means they fired a gun | It means they were all very tall | It means they were scared of the rain
test: «The glass in the car was bulletproof.» What does bulletproof mean? | *Able to stop bullets from going through | Covered in paint | Very cold to touch | Easy to break
test: Jayden says his maths answer is bulletproof, so he is very sure it is right. What does bulletproof mean in his talk? | Rusty and old | Easy to break | Made of metal | *Very reliable and certain
exam: In «some believed their rituals made them bulletproof», which clue shows the idea may not have been agreed on by everyone? | The word «took» in Beijing | *The word «believed», which shows some people thought it | The number 1900 | Nothing, the word is easy
